# Line endings are part of the contract here, not a preference.
#
# AUDIT 2026-08-02. Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` — the default on a
# Windows install — rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout. The test
# suites read the repo's own files and match on `\n`, so on a fresh Windows
# clone tests fail that pass everywhere else. Measured on this repo: a branch
# switch rewrote README.md to 662 CRLF endings and zero LF, and two README
# tests went from passing to failing without a single character of content
# changing.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises in the index AND checks out LF on every
# platform, so what a contributor's editor sees is what the tests read.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
